## _flags.soar -- selection-world: 2 elaborations.

## Elaborate flags default iterative-step -> sets iterative-step.
## operator: an iterative step is a task operator; tie-impasse: it is a tie impasse.
sp {selection-world*elaborate*flags*default*iterative-step
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^flags <f>
             -^flag-override.iterative-step <any>)
-->
   (<f> ^iterative-step operator)   # v2.34: tie-impasse loses where every step is a choice; set per task (probe_settings.py)
}

## Elaborate flags default init-evaluation-depth -> sets init-evaluation-depth.
## one: start at depth 1; unachieved-desireds: start at the number of unachieved desireds (2 when there are 2 or fewer).
## v2.45: the default is unachieved-desireds (JL, 20 Nov 2026); a task where one operator can achieve several desireds sets one.
sp {selection-world*elaborate*flags*default*init-evaluation-depth
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^flags <f>
             -^flag-override.init-evaluation-depth <any>)
-->
   (<f> ^init-evaluation-depth unachieved-desireds)
}

## Elaborate flags default max-evaluation-depth -> sets max-evaluation-depth (v2.37; the value was fixed in the rules before).
## The depth at which iterative deepening stops and achieved-max-depth breaks the tie. Not used with iterative-step cost (1000).
sp {selection-world*elaborate*flags*default*max-evaluation-depth
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^flags <f>
             -^flag-override.max-evaluation-depth <any>)
-->
   (<f> ^max-evaluation-depth 12)
}

## Elaborate flags default max-look-ahead-steps -> 1000 (v2.47).
## A backstop for runaway subgoaling or search inside one evaluation: an evaluation whose look-ahead path has applied this
## many operators ends as depth-exceeded (evaluate-operator/exceed-depth.soar). With iterative-step tie-impasse the depth
## limit counts only tie impasses, so an evaluation that never ties again was unbounded (Soar - To-do row 42). Long chains
## of inference inside one evaluation are legitimate (KenKen 6x6: up to 233 operators after one guess), so the default
## is far above them; a task that knows its bound sets ^flag-override.max-look-ahead-steps.
sp {selection-world*elaborate*flags*default*max-look-ahead-steps
   :default
   (state <s> ^superstate nil
              ^flags <f>
             -^flag-override.max-look-ahead-steps <any>)
-->
   (<f> ^max-look-ahead-steps 1000)
}
